Force bolt has a further problem - it often tends to wake up
nymphs.  And worse when used on nymphs it tends to break
their mirror and reduce luck.  Once I used that I started using
dagger to clear out the initial monsters on each level then
practice force bolt on new appearances and close doors.

One strategy I use with spells early on is based on the fact
that wizards eventually get hunger free casting based on
increased (intelligence I think).  I use the lowest cost spell
in a school and only cast it until I get offered to enhance it
once.  Then I practice more once I have extra levels.

> Skilled magic missile, too.

Because of the hunger and the nymphs, force bolt needs to
start out as a backup weapon to avoid melee not the first
choice.

