> > weapon. Wield an elven dagger

One thing I did was write down all of the skill classes I could
eventually max out then start crossing them out.  I ended up
noticing that I could max out all of the spell schools, plus dagger
to expert, plus either broadsword or long sword as a possible
crowning gift to basic, plus polearm to skilled and nothing else.
Very cool.  Then I figured spend every slot on dagger until it
hits expert and after that pretty much anything else in almost
any other order.  Machine gun dagger.

> And #name it Sting even if you're Neutral; the orc warning and web-cutting
> is useful and it doesn't cost anything. It doesn't hurt your chance of
> Magicbane from sacrifice either.

Because I often can't completely avoid melee I will even name
Sting if my wizard is chaotic.  The only weapons I keep interest
in is my stack of daggers, my wielded Sting/Magicbane, a
backup mean artifact alternate wield, a polearm for the two
castles.  As a chaotic I might chose Orcrist in hopes of
eventually getting Stormy as my alternate wield early on.  As
a neutral I might chose a regular long sword or any artifact
long sword as my alternate wield in hopes of eventually getting
Frosty or Vorpy.

My weapons continue to be first daggers, second force bolt,
third wielded dagger, last the alternate wield larger weapon.

